wip/mlx: Import mlx-0.32.4

MLX is Apple's NumPy-like array framework for machine learning on
Apple silicon, with lazy evaluation, automatic differentiation and a
Metal GPU backend.  This package holds the C++ library.

Command Line Tools lack the offline metal shader compiler, which MLX
uses even in JIT mode for its version probe, its JIT source generation
and 13 always-precompiled kernel files.  A patched-in option,
MLX_METAL_RUNTIME_COMPILE, removes that need.  It embeds those kernel
sources and compiles them at run time through the Metal API, so no
mlx.metallib is installed.

A second patch fixes an upstream bug in JIT mode.  The head-dim split
NAX attention kernel got one template argument too many, so it failed
to compile for head dims 256 and 512.
